\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{The volume element and the cell parity}
\date{2026-11-23}

\p{In positive even dimension the volume element #{C} of
\ref{fdip-009X} is a [grading](fdip-013N) of #{S\otimes F},
acting pointwise on fields. The invertible generator
#{\varepsilon_1^S\otimes\bbI_F} interchanges its eigenspaces,
which therefore have equal dimension. The covariant centered
operator #{D_{a,U}} is odd for this grading.}

\p{On [based cochains](fdip-00SH) over a field of characteristic
different from #{2}, the cell parity acts by #{(-1)^p} in degree
#{p}. Its super-dimension is the even-minus-odd rank difference
of \ref{fdip-00T0}. Both #{\extd} and #{\extdag} change parity,
so #{\extd+\extdag} is odd.}
